<section
	data-testid="about"
	id="problem"
	class="flex flex-col items-start justify-center py-20 lg:py-32"
>
	<h2 class="mb-2 font-monospace text-2xl text-orange lg:text-4xl">The Problem</h2>
	<span class="mb-8 h-1 w-10 bg-orange"></span>

	<div class="max-w-2xl text-black dark:text-white">
		<p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
			Moving to a new city means eating alone — a lot. Communal dishes like hotpot and dim sum lose
			their appeal without company. Existing platforms like Meetup handle large events, but nothing
			exists for the simple, recurring need: finding one to three people to share a meal with.
		</p>

		<blockquote
			class="border-l-4 border-orange pl-5 py-2 text-xl font-semibold italic text-black dark:text-white"
		>
			"People don't want a dining companion who likes the same food. They want someone they can
			actually talk to."
			<span class="mt-2 block text-sm font-normal not-italic text-orange">
				— Core insight from user research
			</span>
		</blockquote>
	</div>
</section>
